  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed on a vertical fixed circular track and then it is given velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;along the track&nbsp;at position&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> on track. The coefficient of friction between the block and the track varies with the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math>.&nbsp;If the block moves on track with constant speed then the coefficient of friction is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0111_3986d309d0cf.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 114px;\" />"
  },
